 "Desert of Dangling Pointers": "",
 "A new road, a new quest. Your pet is ready.": "",
 "The Sleepy Meadow": "",
 "Your pet stretches, looks at the road, then at you. An adventure starts.": "",
 "Dunes of Deprecation": "",
 "Old tools lie half-buried in the sand. Some still bite.": "",
 "The Dungeon of Daemons": "",
 "Deep below, processes that never die guard the way.": "",
 "Pipes": "",
 "A pipe | sends the output of one command into the next one.": "",
 "Chain small tools, one step each.": "",
 "Read it left to right: filter, keep what you need, then count.": "",
 "awk, the column reader": "",
 "awk reads a file line by line and cuts each line into fields: $1 is the first word, $2 the second, $NF the last.": "",
 "-F sets the separator, for CSV and friends.": "",
 "A condition before the braces picks lines; END runs after the last one.": "",
 "3-command pipes": "",
 "finish chapter 1 of bashou adventure": "",
 "Log Hydra": "",
 "The Log Hydra grows a head for every [ERROR] line in app.log.\nHow many lines contain [ERROR]? (lowercase \"error\" doesn't count)": "",
 "grep can count matching lines by itself: look at `grep -c`.": "",
 "Try: grep -c '\\[ERROR\\]' app.log  (or grep -cF '[ERROR]' app.log)": "",
 "Ledger Golem": "",
 "The Ledger Golem only yields to exact accounts.\nIn sales.csv, what is the total qty (3rd column) sold for \"{item}\"?": "",
 "awk splits lines into fields: -F, sets the separator, $2 and $3 are the columns.": "",
 "Try: awk -F, '$2 == \"ITEM\" { s += $3 } END { print s }' sales.csv": "",
 "Maze Wraith": "",
 "The Maze Wraith hides in backup files.\nHow many regular files ending in .bak are there in maze/, at any depth?\n(Careful: some directories are named *.bak too.)": "",
 "find walks every subdirectory; -type f keeps only files, -name matches a pattern.": "",
 "Try: find maze -type f -name '*.bak' | wc -l": "",
 "Echo Swarm": "",
 "The Echo Swarm repeats itself endlessly.\nWhich IP address appears most often in visitors.txt?": "",
 "uniq only merges adjacent lines, so sort first. `uniq -c` counts them.": "",
 "Try: sort visitors.txt | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -1": "",
 "Typo Serpent": "",
 "The Typo Serpent scrambled letter.txt: \"the\" became \"teh\" in places.\nFix the file in place (every occurrence, also \"Teh\"), then type: answer done": "",
 "sed -i edits a file in place; s/old/new/g replaces every match on a line.": "",
 "Try: sed -i 's/teh/the/g; s/Teh/The/g' letter.txt": "",
 "Process Phantom": "",
 "A Process Phantom named {name} haunts this machine.\nWhat is its PID?": "",
 "`ps aux` lists every process with its PID in the 2nd column; filter it with grep.": "",
 "Try: pgrep -f phantom   or   ps aux | grep phantom": "",
 "Knot Eel": "",
 "The Knot Eel ties commands into knots. Untie it with one pipeline of at least 3 commands.\nIn access.log (ip, method, page, status), how many different IPs got a 404 status?": "",
 "One small step per command, joined with |: keep the 404 lines, keep the IP, drop duplicates, count.": "",
 "Try: grep ' 404$' access.log | cut -d' ' -f1 | sort -u | wc -l": "",
 "Hidden file": "",
 "Someone left a hidden file in this folder. What is the word inside it?": "",
 "`ls` doesn't show files whose name starts with a dot. `ls -a` does.": "",
 "Try: ls -a, then cat the file that starts with a dot.": "",
 "Encoded note": "",
 "note.txt looks like gibberish, but it's only encoded, not encrypted.\nDecode it: what is the password?": "",
 "Letters, digits, + and /, sometimes = at the end: that's base64.": "",
 "Try: base64 -d note.txt": "",
 "Brute force": "",
 "Someone is trying passwords on this server's SSH.\nIn auth.log, which IP address has the most failed logins?": "",
 "Keep only the \"Failed password\" lines first: grep. Then keep the IP, count, sort.": "",
 "Try: grep 'Failed password' auth.log | awk '{print $(NF-3)}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -3": "",
 "Defaced site": "",
 "An intruder changed one file of the website in site/ a few minutes ago.\nEvery other file is weeks old. Which file was changed?": "",
 "`find` can filter by modification time: -mmin -10 means \"less than 10 minutes ago\".": "",
 "Try: find site -type f -mmin -10  (or: ls -lt site/*)": "",
 "Cron backdoor": "",
 "One of the scheduled jobs in etc/cron.d is a backdoor: it downloads a script and runs it.\nWhat domain does it download from?": "",
 "Look for a download piped into a shell: curl … | sh. grep -r searches every file.": "",
 "Try: grep -r '| *sh' etc/cron.d": "",
 "SUID file": "",
 "On a real system, a SUID program runs as its owner (often root), whoever starts it.\nOne program in bin/ has the SUID bit set. Which one?": "",
 "`ls -l` shows an s instead of x in the owner's permissions: -rwsr-xr-x.": "",
 "Try: find bin -perm -4000  (or: ls -l bin)": "",
 "Locked chest": "",
 "Build the camp: create the folders {path} (all of them, in one command).": "",
 "mkdir creates a folder; one option creates the missing parents too.": "",
 "Try: mkdir -p {path}": "",
 "Leave a trail: create the file map.txt containing the word {word}.": "",
 "echo prints a word, > sends it into a file.": "",
 "Try: echo {word} > map.txt": "",
 "Put the key (key.txt) into the chest/ folder.": "",
 "mv moves a file (and renames it).": "",
 "Try: mv key.txt chest/": "",
 "Make a backup: copy the folder scroll/ with everything in it to backup/.": "",
 "cp copies files; folders need an option to copy what's inside.": "",
 "Try: cp -r scroll backup": "",
 "Polish the sword: rename rusty_sword.txt to shiny_sword.txt.": "",
 "The same command moves and renames.": "",
 "Try: mv rusty_sword.txt shiny_sword.txt": "",
 "Sweep the camp: remove every .tmp file, keep the .txt ones.": "",
 "rm removes files; *.tmp matches every name ending in .tmp.": "",
 "Try: rm *.tmp": "",
 "Make spell.sh runnable, then run it (./spell.sh).": "",
 "A file needs the x permission to be run.": "",
 "Try: chmod u+x spell.sh && ./spell.sh": "",
 "Make a shortcut: a symbolic link named home that points to camp/tent.": "",
 "ln makes links; one option makes a symbolic (soft) link.": "",
 "Try: ln -s camp/tent home": "",
 "Write in the journal: add the line rested at the end of journal.txt, without erasing it.": "",
 ">> appends, > would replace the whole file.": "",
 "Try: echo rested >> journal.txt": "",
 "How many .gem files are hidden in cave/, at any depth? Then: answer <number>": "",
 "find searches every folder below; wc -l counts lines.": "",
 "Try: find cave -name '*.gem' | wc -l": "",
 "Pack the loot: put the folder loot/ into a compressed archive loot.tar.gz.": "",
 "tar: c creates, z compresses with gzip, f names the archive.": "",
 "Try: tar czf loot.tar.gz loot": "",
 "Make peace: in letter.txt, replace every dragon with friend (edit the file in place).": "",
 "sed can edit a file in place; g replaces every match on a line.": "",
 "Try: sed -i 's/dragon/friend/g' letter.txt": "",
 "One scroll in library/ talks about the treasure. Which file? Then: answer <file name>": "",
 "grep -r searches every file below a folder; -l prints only the file names.": "",
 "Try: grep -rl treasure library": "",
 "people.txt has a name, an age and a city per line. Make names.txt with only the names, one per line.": "",
 "awk '{print $1}' prints the first field; > writes it to a file.": "",
 "Try: awk '{print $1}' people.txt > names.txt": "",
 "prices.txt has an item and a price per line. What's the total? Then: answer <number>": "",
 "awk can add up a column in a variable and print it in END.": "",
 "Try: awk '{s += $2} END {print s}' prices.txt": "",
 "How many different cities are in people.txt (3rd column)? Then: answer <number>": "",
 "Keep the city column, remove duplicates, count the lines: three commands joined with |.": "",
 "Try: awk '{print $3}' people.txt | sort -u | wc -l": ""
}
